    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-060: Eliminate string-copy overhead in layout hot path**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (~100 lines, 3 files) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\nUses the 1099-sample perf profile to target the **25.13% `fill_sides` lambda** and **~9.5% allocation churn**. Expected layout win: **10–15% (~250-370ms off 2678ms median)**.\n\n## The measurement driving this\n\n**Baseline (Release, median-of-3 Wikipedia):** layout **2678ms**, cascade 263ms.\n\n**perf record `-g --call-graph dwarf`, 1099 samples:**\n\n| Symbol | Self % | Attribution |\n|---|---|---|\n| `contains_word` | 5.19% | **Cascade** — `.class` substring match |\n| `pthread_rwlock_unlock` | 3.15% | Library internal |\n| `_int_free` / `malloc` / `_int_*` | **9.5%** | **Allocation churn** |\n| `do_lookup_x` | 1.75% | Linker (first-load, **ignore**) |\n| `FcCharSetIsSubset` | 1.49% | Fontconfig |\n| `matches_simple` / `matches_from` | 2.64% | Cascade-side |\n| `__memmove_evex` | 1.29% | String copies |\n\n**Cumulative report (`--children`):**\n\n```\n34.87%  layout_element (whole layout phase)\n  |-25.13%  fill_sides lambda  ← TARGET\n  |-12.79%  recursive layout_element calls\n  |-~10%    box sizing, transform, background\n```\n\n## The 25.13% target\n\n`fill_sides` (`layout.cpp:37-44`), called 12× per element (margin ×4, padding ×4, border-width ×4). Each call:\n\n1. **Key allocation** — caller passes `const char*`, `get()` takes `const std::string&` (implicit alloc)\n2. **Map lookup** — hash + compare\n3. **Value copy** — `get()` returns `optional<string>`, copies `CascadeValue::value`\n\n**12 calls × 5000 elements = 60K lookups, 120K string allocations** per Wikipedia render.\n\n## Two honest corrections to initial hypotheses\n\n### 1. \"Inline `is_ws` in selectors.cpp\" — WRONG\n\nI initially proposed this as a ~5% win, assuming it called `std::isspace`. **It doesn't** — `is_ws` (selectors.cpp:576-578) is already a simple char-comparison chain. **Dropped from scope.**\n\n### 2. \"`contains_word` is layout-side\" — WRONG\n\n`contains_word` at 5.19% is **cascade-side** (runs during `SelectorList::matches`). Post-ADR-059, cascade is only 7% of total. Even 2× speedup saves ~2%. **Deferred to ADR-061** (cascade optimization), not this ADR.\n\n**The diagnostic's most valuable output was disproving my own hypotheses.** ADR-060's scope is derived entirely from the profile, not from speculation.\n\n## What ships (2 focused fixes, read-path only)\n\n### Fix 1: `ComputedStyle::get_view()`\n\n`string_view`-returning variant alongside existing `get()`. Uses C++20 transparent hash/equal for heterogeneous lookup:\n\n```cpp\nstruct ComputedStyle {\n    std::unordered_map<std::string, CascadeValue, StringHash, StringEq> declarations;\n    std::optional<std::string_view> get_view(std::string_view property) const;\n    // get() unchanged — existing callers keep working\n};\n```\n\n### Fix 2: `fill_sides` inline fast path\n\n```cpp\n// Before: 2 allocs (key + value copy)\nauto px = [&](const char* p) {\n    const auto v = style->get(p);\n    return v ? parse_length(*v, ctx) : 0.0f;\n};\n\n// After: zero allocs (transparent hash + reference access)\nauto px = [&](std::string_view p) -> float {\n    auto it = style->declarations.find(p);\n    if (it == style->declarations.end()) return 0.0f;\n    return parse_length(it->second.value, ctx);\n};\n```\n\n**Same behavior, three costs eliminated** — key alloc, value copy, optional wrapper.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n**`get_view()` is ADDITIVE, not replacing `get()`** — some callers need owned strings (`value_or` patterns). Additive keeps blast radius small.\n\n**Transparent hash is universal** — every `get_view(string_view)` call site benefits without per-callsite static keys. Alternative (static const strings) would work for `fill_sides` but not other callers.\n\n**Typed `ComputedStyle` fields (the bigger fix) are ADR-061** — ~200 lines, changes data model, touches cascade population. Ship ADR-060's incremental wins first to prove the methodology.\n\n## What the fix does NOT eliminate\n\n- **`unordered_map::find` hash + compare** — still happens per lookup\n- **`parse_length` cost** — still happens per property (not in top-10 profile, defer)\n- **`get()` for callers that need owned strings** — correct, they need the copy\n\n**That's why estimate is 10-15%, not 25%.** The remaining 10% requires typed fields (ADR-061).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- 3 new `get_view` tests: return value matches `get()`, `nullopt` for missing, `const char*` literal works\n- Median-of-3 `PERF-LAYOUT` on Wikipedia (pre: 2678ms)\n- **Success criterion**: layout median < 2420ms (10% win)\n- `PERF-CASCADE` should be unchanged (~193ms)\n\n## Deferred\n\n- **Typed `ComputedStyle` fields** — ADR-061\n- **`contains_word` optimization** — cascade-side, ADR-061/062\n- **`parse_length` fast path** — not in top-10 profile\n- **`pthread_rwlock` (4.82%)** — library-internal (GTK/glib/fontconfig), not actionable\n- **`FcCharSetIsSubset` (1.49%)** — fontconfig, defer unless text-heavy pages need more\n\nRefs #260\n",
